                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in Mr. McHenry’s note of June 30,
                        1879.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">the united kingdom of great britain and
                        ireland.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Answers to Mr. Welsh’s
                        questions.</hi></p>
                <p>There is no gold or silver coin or bullion in the treasury, excepting a small
                    amount for petty cash. All the government receipts and payments are made through
                    the Bank of England, including salaries, which are paid quarterly.</p>
