                <p>It is impossible to tell what quantity of gold and silver is consumed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">annually</hi> in the arts and manufactures. There are no
                    reliable data in respect thereto.</p>
                <p>The excess of <hi rendition="#italic">gold</hi> imports over exports, 1858 to
                    1878, may thus be accounted for: <table cols="2" rows="6">
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell>Increase in circulation, say</cell>
                            <cell role="num">£43,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Increase in stock of bullion, say</cell>
                            <cell role="num">5,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Gold plate manufactured, say</cell>
                            <cell role="num">2,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Arts and manufactures, say</cell>
                            <cell role="num">20,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Emigrants and other passengers, say</cell>
                            <cell rendition="#border-bottom" role="num">17,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell role="num">87,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
                <p>The excess of <hi rendition="#italic">silver</hi> imports over exports, 1858 to
                    1878, may thus be accounter for: <table cols="2" rows="3">
